meta { name: Create a draft, type: http, seq: 2 }

post { url: {{adminBase}}/articles, body: json, auth: none }

headers { Cookie: {{sessionCookie}} }

body:json {
  {
    "title": "A draft written from Bruno"
  }
}

docs {
  Always creates a DRAFT — there is no path that creates something already
  public. The slug is derived from the title unless you send one.

  Authorship comes from the SESSION. Adding "authorId" here returns 400:
  forbidNonWhitelisted rejects unknown fields, which is what stops a contributor
  publishing under someone else's byline.

  Sending the same title twice returns 409 ARTICLE_DUPLICATE_SLUG — but the same
  slug in the OTHER tenant is fine, and that is the point.
}
